Me:
why do we do astype str before replacing dollar signs in pandas, isnt Amount already a string

AI:
When pandas reads a CSV it tries to guess the data type of each column. If the Amount column contains values like 69.99 with no dollar signs it might read it as a float, not a string. In that case calling .str.replace on it would fail with an AttributeError because floats do not have string methods.

Using .astype(str) first guarantees that every value in the column is converted to a string before the regex runs. So 69.99 the float becomes "69.99" the string, and -15.0 the float becomes "-15.0" the string. The regex then runs without errors regardless of what pandas guessed the original column type was.

In Google Colab reading CSV files with dollar signs, pandas typically reads Amount as a string already. But astype(str) is a defensive measure that makes the function work correctly in all situations.

