Me:
why do we need global chat_history, what happens without it

AI:
Without the global declaration, Python treats chat_history inside the function as a local variable. When you call chat_history.append() Python looks for a local variable called chat_history, does not find one, and raises an UnboundLocalError. With global chat_history, Python knows to use the chat_history list defined outside the function. The append modifies that shared list so conversation history persists across multiple calls to the function.

